Iquerayable vs Ienumerable 

IQueryable ka kaam hai: SQL Database se baat karna aur wahi par filter lagana taaki network par faltu data na aaye.

IEnumerable ka kaam hai: Ek aam universal collection contract dena, taaki poori application me kahin bhi (chahe DB ho, File ho, ya Memory list ho) 
data ko aaram se pass kiya ja sake aur loop chalaya ja sake.

List<string> realList = new List<string> { "Apple", "Banana" };

// Humne iska ek IEnumerable view bana liya
IEnumerable<string> readOnlyView = realList; 
// readOnlyView.Add("Mango"); // ❌ Error! Kyunki IEnumerable ke paas Add method nahi hai.

// LEKIN doosra banda agar asli list me add kar de:
realList.Add("Mango"); 

// Toh readOnlyView me bhi "Mango" apne aap dikhne lagega!
